From: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:43:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mm/damon/core: reset damos quota charge pointers for removed
 target/region

damos_quota->charge_{target,addr}_from saves the target and region the
scheme's quota limit is reached.  damos_skip_charged_region() skips the
target and regions before the point.  The target that assigned to
charge_target_from could be removed from the context in runtime, via
damon_commit_ctx().  In the case, damos_skip_charged_region() cannot
find if the point is passed or not, so the scheme is effectively
disabled.  In addition to the scenario, a new target that coincidently
having the address same to charge_target_from can dynamically added.
Then the skip logic can work again.  But, if the target has no region,
again the skip pointer cannot be found because
damos_skip_charged_region() is called for each region.

No critical issues like crash or leak happens.  Users could work around
by re-installing scheme.  Users could surprise and confused from the
sudden stop of DAMOS works, though.

Handle the corner cases in damos_adjust_quota() and reset the pointers.

Fixes: da87878010e5 ("mm/damon/sysfs: support online inputs update")
Cc: <stable@vger.kernel.org> # 5.19.x
Closes: https://sashiko.dev/#/bug/linux-cd0c55fc-0cc8-45d8-9637-3334811c49b8
Signed-off-by: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
---
 mm/damon/core.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mm/damon/core.c b/mm/damon/core.c
index 831e8eb135ea3..d4aa691c846a6 100644
--- a/mm/damon/core.c
+++ b/mm/damon/core.c
@@ -3607,6 +3607,32 @@ static void damos_trace_esz(struct damon_ctx *c, struct damos *s,
 	trace_damos_esz(cidx, sidx, quota->esz);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Target that set to charge_target_from could be dynamically removed via
+ * damon_commit_ctx().  A target having no region could be dynamically added
+ * and coincidently have the address same to charge_target_from.  Catch the
+ * conrner cases and reset charge_{target,addr}_from.
+ */
+static void damos_reset_charge_from_pointers(struct damon_ctx *c,
+		struct damos *s)
+{
+	struct damos_quota *quota;
+	struct damon_target *t;
+
+	quota = &s->quota;
+	if (!quota->charge_target_from)
+		return;
+	damon_for_each_target(t, c) {
+		if (t == quota->charge_target_from) {
+			if (damon_nr_regions(t) > 0)
+				return;
+			break;
+		}
+	}
+	quota->charge_target_from = NULL;
+	quota->charge_addr_from = 0;
+}
+
 static void damos_adjust_quota(struct damon_ctx *c, struct damos *s)
 {
 	struct damos_quota *quota = &s->quota;
@@ -3647,6 +3673,8 @@ static void damos_adjust_quota(struct damon_ctx *c, struct damos *s)
 			damos_trace_esz(c, s, quota);
 	}
 
+	damos_reset_charge_from_pointers(c, s);
+
 	if (damos_quota_is_full(quota, c->min_region_sz))
 		return;
 	if (!c->ops.get_scheme_score)
-- 
